IMPORT prelude

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (Australia): PART 9, the subsection pass 1 left unencoded (pass 2).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Section 40A(4) does not say whether a provision of the old legislation corresponds to one of the new:
-- it says which other Part of which other Act answers the question. Pass 1 read that as "refers to another Act", which is not a ground
-- for leaving a provision out. It is encoded as a pointer, and the answer to the question itself is an INPUT, as in the borrowed
-- definitions of Part 2. The rule for s 40A(1) to (3) and (5) is in au-part9-citation.l4.

§ `Part 9: Citation of Acts and instruments (section 40A(4))`

§§ `Section 40A(4): where correspondence is decided`

DECLARE `Old legislation` IS ONE OF
    `the old corporations legislation`
    `the old ASIC legislation`

-- src:869 | (4) For the purposes of this section:
-- src:870 | (a) the question whether a part, provision or provisions of the old corporations legislation corresponds to a part, provision or provisions of the new corporations legislation is to be determined in the same way as it is determined for the purposes of Part 10.1 of the Corporations Act 2001; and
-- src:871 | (b) the question whether a part, provision or provisions of the old ASIC legislation corresponds to a part, provision or provisions of the new ASIC legislation is to be determined in the same way as it is determined for the purposes of Part 16 of the Australian Securities and Investments Commission Act 2001.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 40A(4) (src:869-871)
GIVEN old IS A `Old legislation`
GIVETH A STRING
`the Part that decides whether a provision of the old legislation corresponds to one of the new` old MEANS
    CONSIDER old
    WHEN `the old corporations legislation` THEN "Part 10.1 of the Corporations Act 2001"
    WHEN `the old ASIC legislation` THEN "Part 16 of the Australian Securities and Investments Commission Act 2001"

-- Whether that Part treats the two provisions as corresponding is an INPUT: it is not in the text.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 40A(4) (src:869-871)
GIVEN `the Part that subsection (4) points at treats the provisions as corresponding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the old provision corresponds to the new provision for section 40A` `the Part that subsection (4) points at treats the provisions as corresponding` MEANS
    `the Part that subsection (4) points at treats the provisions as corresponding`
